ong Technology peers, with revenue growing 181%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $276K per employee reflects an ownership culture. Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["IonQ, Inc. is a large-cap technology business with a $11.6B market cap on $130M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -53% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at -92% against a 12% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $300M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, interest coverage of 40\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Net dilution runs at 28.7% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and stock-based comp at 240% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Technology peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Technology peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 494% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text"